Q: Can not use $rename to rename property of documents A: <p>You cant use <code>$rename</code> after you already changed the field name in schema</p>
<p><code>$rename</code> works only on existing fields in db.</p>
<p>So first keep the old name in schema, run <code>$rename</code> in db:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>await Document.updateMany(
  { templateType: { $exists: true } },
  { $rename: { templateType: &quot;documentType&quot; } }
);
</code></pre>
<p>After all docs updated, you can update schema to new name. This way <code>$rename</code> finds the field and works properly.</p>
